<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="37001" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png" data-orig-size="1592,1322" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-37001" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=500" alt="April-May 2015 neighborhood dmage.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png 1592w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=150&amp;h=125 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=300&amp;h=249 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=768&amp;h=638 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/april-may-2015-neighborhood-dmage.png?w=1024&amp;h=850 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1592px) 100vw, 1592px" /></p>
<p><em>Neighborhood Damage in Aleppo, April-May 2015/<a href="http://reliefweb.int/sites/reliefweb.int/files/resources/UNOSAT_A3_Aleppo_Percent_Neighbourhood.pdf">UNOSAT</a></em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><em><img data-attachment-id="36965" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/nostat-bomb-famage-level/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png" data-orig-size="2120,1360" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="nostat-bomb-famage-level" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36965" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=500" alt="nostat Bomb Famage Level.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png 2120w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=150&amp;h=96 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=300&amp;h=192 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=768&amp;h=493 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nostat-bomb-famage-level.png?w=1024&amp;h=657 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 2120px) 100vw, 2120px" />Building Damage Assessment:  Red-Destroyed; Tan-Severe; Yellow-Moderate; February 18 2016 New York <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/world/middleeast/aleppo-syria-airstrikes.html">Times</a>/<a href="http://reliefweb.int/map/syrian-arab-republic/neighborhood-damage-percentages-aleppo-syria-18-feb-2016">UNOSAT data</a></em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Not only has the scope of bomb damage spread across much of the Old City and even to Western Aleppo, in contrast with the images of earlier years, but the bombs have been dropped with intensity around the Citadel, the Airport, and more recently the old industrial area and northwestern outskirts, as the siege of Aleppo adopts a broad basis and intensifies around relatively similar combat lines on the ground.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>6.  The escalation of air bombings of Aleppo followed the huge surprise of the destruction of a convoy of volunteer relief workers and their supplies.  Indeed, the near-continuous bombardment of the cross-line convoy of Red Crescent volunteers who stopped at Oram al-Kubra outside Aleppo last week, along the highway running from Damascus to Aleppo, not only led to an immediate <a class="u-underline" href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/sep/20/un-suspends-all-aid-convoy-movements-in-syria-after-airstrike">suspension of all aid deliveries across Syria</a> and destroyed any optimism and good-will that the cease-fire had generated and peace initiative sought to foster.  It seemed a rehearsal for the bombing of the city.  Shortly after the public mourning of Omar Baraka, coordinator of the convoy who was killed in the attacks, who had &#8220;sacrificed his money, time &amp; effort to ease suffering of all the needy in Aleppo province,&#8221; a moment of shock difficult to process, ramped up raids on Aleppo began, in ways that may seem increasingly controlled less from Damascus than Moscow.</p>
<p>The attack on the convoy that was shocking in itself as an attack on civilians who had risked their lives to help war victims with Red Crescent, taking clear aim at supplies destined for Aleppo.  It now appears but the preface to a dramatic expansion of a theater of war that was already intent on creating food shortages and rendering the lives of those in Aleppo impossible, and to persuade &#8220;militants&#8221; who challenge the Assad regime to lay down their weapons and leave the city.  Indeed, raids over the next days targeted hospitals, food lines, medical centers, power centers and residential neighborhoods in Aleppo, as well as in Homs, Idlib Province, and Ar Raqqah, in a reign of terror from the skies.  It makes one wonder what Russian allies of the regime, who seem to have brought renewed fire-power of prohibited bunker-buster bombs to the city&#8217;s siege, seek to gain in the total destruction of much of the city&#8211;and to isolate it from Damascus and future aid, before they decided to enter the eastern part of the city with tanks at the end of the first week of October 2016, to try to claim control of the city.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36141" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/khanasser-road/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png" data-orig-size="1302,848" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="khanasser-road" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36141" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=500" alt="khanasser-road"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png 1302w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=150&amp;h=98 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=300&amp;h=195 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=768&amp;h=500 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=1024&amp;h=667 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1302px) 100vw, 1302px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>What seemed a unicum of horror is now, perhaps, a sign of a change in strategy in a broad theater of war.  The deadly surprise attack on a convoy of <a class="internallink" href="http://www.aljazeera.com/news/2016/09/syria-deadly-aid-convoy-bombing-ceasefire-ends-160919194433498.html" target="_self">thirty-one vehicles including eighteen UN aid trucks</a> bearing emergency supplies and food hit over several hours by thirty aerial bombs  in the late evening hours of September 20 destroyed not only many of the very trucks bearing food and other needed supplies&#8211;including blankets and winter clothes, intended for civilians stranded in war-torn Aleppo, Syria&#8217;s largest city as recently as 2011&#8211;as successive fireballs killed twenty-one civilian volunteers from Arab Red Crescent.  Traveling along the Aleppo Supply Road by recognized routes, the convoy was cleared for travel, albeit with the specific request it not be accompanied by United Nations staff, who had given the exact coordinates of the journey of the convoy to the Syrian government which was falsely accused of bringing supplies to terrorists, although the convoy had been fully examined and cleared for departure.</p>
<p>Although the cease-fire had aimed to stop the airborne delivery of barrel bombs loaded with TNT&#8211;bombs prohibited by the United Nations, but central to the offensive of the Syrian Government Army on the city from the battle&#8217;s start&#8211;that forced many to leave the city that once held 2.5 million inhabitants, it has given way to a more intensified bombing than Aleppo or other cities in Syria have encountered.  In part, the raids of Russian planes are just dropping more bombs&#8211;destroying neighborhoods from 300 feet overhead, with up to fifty planes, each carrying two bombs, targeting residents of Aleppo each day and intentionally destroying its increasingly frayed fabric.  Already by late 2013, witnesses in Old Aleppo had <a href="http://english.aawsat.com/2013/12/article55325898">experienced</a> an earlier escalation from assault by helicopters to heavier bombardment by military aircraft&#8211;whose increased delivery of barrel bombs created a new landscape of devastation in the city.  But the increasing aim at underground passage-ways and hospitals&#8211;as well as lines of bread and industry&#8211;ratchets up the siege to a full war, as if a new Stalingrad.  The escalation of violence against civilians and attacks on supplies in the city may have begun from the attack on the convoy, inaugurating a new phase in the mapping of the war that was coordinated not only by the Syrian government, but that seems to have dramatically expanded a different and still unknown scope.</p>
<p>While the convoy was eager to leave in the wake of the cease-fire negotiated, the open attack against its progress received recent attention as an openly brazen war crime&#8211;a continuous bombardment of peace-keeping civilians intentionally destroying needed provisions for citizens, leaving only wreckage as the sun rose the next day.  “<em>They want to kill humanity</em>,&#8221; said a colleague of the Red Crescent worker who coordinated the cross-line convoy, “<em>but humanity will not die</em>.”  For Aleppo, if a shell of its former self, had been a long center for anti-Assad protests, has been the longest and largest theater of urban warfare in the Civil War, a convergence of elite military and local ethnic militias, as well as foreign Islamic fighters and Mujahideen, tied to rebel groups but not committed to overthrowing Assad, but encouraging a recent push to cut off all supply routes to the rebel-held parts of the city and starve them out by cutting off the arrival of goods to Eastern Aleppo on the highways and Castello Road, as rebels have tried to open new supply lines to the city.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><em><img data-attachment-id="36722" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/attachment/3300/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg" data-orig-size="1920,1152" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="3300" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36722 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=500" alt="3300.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg 1920w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=150&amp;h=90 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=300&amp;h=180 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=768&amp;h=461 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3300.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=614 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" />Ammar Abdullah/Reuters</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Fears of a massacre of the city&#8217;s civilian population have been present from 2012.  Aleppo has remained among the most bombarded war-torn cities in Syria, and one of the regions in which the power of the current government of Bashar al-Assad is trying to retain.  The outpost of the Syrian army&#8211;and has been transformed as it has become a theater of violence over five years.  Russia continues to deny any responsibility for the attacks of September 20&#8211;or involvement of airplanes in the strike&#8211;and have deflected guilt for the strikes which they preposterously call a propaganda stunt by the United States government, but also targeted multiple <a href="http://www.syriahr.com/en/?p=50837">sites along the road to Aleppo</a>, wounding multiple civilians and destroying buildings that may conceal other dead.  Earlier helicopter raids had dropped barrel bombs <a href="http://www.syriahr.com/en/?p=50837">in the Hama countryside</a>, and much of the <a href="http://www.syriahr.com/en/?p=50837">southern countryside</a> of Idlib Province this September&#8211;interrupting the Highway on which supplies arrive, if with no known casualties according to the Syrian Observatory of Human Rights.  The September 20 bombing led UN OCHA to negotiate another route to reach Aleppo&#8217;s civilian residents than the route destroyed by further air raids, and forty trucks await on the <a href="http://www.al-monitor.com/pulse/afp/2016/09/syria-conflict-un-aid.html">Syrian -Turkish border</a> for a guarantee of safe passage.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36794" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/attachment/2734/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg" data-orig-size="620,372" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="2734" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36794 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg?w=500" alt="2734.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg 620w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg?w=150&amp;h=90 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2734.jpg?w=300&amp;h=180 300w" sizes="(max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px" /><em>Louai Beshara/AFP/Getty Images</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36741" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg" data-orig-size="570,329" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" wp-image-36741 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg?w=657&#038;h=379" alt="7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a" width="657" height="379" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg 570w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg?w=150&amp;h=87 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/7cf1340a4a47f53b388d1504a2909b2ce49f436a.jpg?w=300&amp;h=173 300w" sizes="(max-width: 657px) 100vw, 657px" /><em>Damaged Medical Supplies at Orum al-Kumbra after the Sept. 20 attack outside of Aleppo              </em><em>Omar Haj Kadour/Agence France-Presses</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Strengthening the virtual stranglehold on the city of Aleppo&#8217;s residents has for five years been tantamount to the Syrian government&#8217;s official policy.  “<em>Let Bashar feed you</em>,” taunted rebel fighters in Aleppo at those in the western part of the city, conscious of the regime&#8217;s artificial constraints on incoming supplies and food that have brought artificial ten-fold price differences in the city&#8217;s eastern and western halves.   Before the five years of civil war, had produced an abundance of wheat and other grains sufficient to export.   As pro-government forces continue to taunt other city residents with texts offering food, blankets, food and medicine to those in the zones of the destroyed city they hold, enforced scarcity of resources has provided a crucial tool to continue a psychological war over the remaining population, which the arrival of supplies would threaten to upend:  a region that once exported an abundance of wheat, barley, and pistachios now struggles to circulate sufficient quantities of bread, in a way where food is an increased currency of exchange since before 2011, when Civil War began, and exports of wheat and barley dropped to a flat-line&#8211;and pistachio exports barely grew, as agricultural exports all but ceased and the scarcity of once-plentiful products grew.  The decreased availability in the city and growing cost of food, medical goods, consumer and health products or blankets for the coming winter in Aleppo now seem created, in a desperate attempt to squeeze those who remain in eastern sectors of the city to compel them to a truce.</p>
<p>Everything collapsed so quickly after the destruction of the convoy, that the later escalation of resumed aerial bombardment seemed previously planned.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>7.  The substitution of a geography of plenty in Aleppo with one of bombed out buildings and dislocated refugees is difficult to grasp or fully comprehend, and surreal.   For the extent of ratcheted up violence on civilian residents over recent weeks have rewritten the landscape of a formerly vibrant city in ways difficult to process psychologically for its residents.</p>
<p>The graphs below cannot map the war of forced starvation, or capture the drama of bombardment of urban infrastructure, but suggest the bizarre shift in the forced increase of scarcity, intensifying existing food shortages created by regional warming.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36159" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/syrian-wheat-exports/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png" data-orig-size="1260,690" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="syrian-wheat-exports" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36159" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=500" alt="syrian-wheat-exports"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png 1260w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=150&amp;h=82 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=300&amp;h=164 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=768&amp;h=421 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-wheat-exports.png?w=1024&amp;h=561 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1260px) 100vw, 1260px" /></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36158" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/syrian-barley/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png" data-orig-size="1242,692" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="syrian-barley" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36158" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=500" alt="syrian-barley"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png 1242w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=150&amp;h=84 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=300&amp;h=167 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=768&amp;h=428 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-barley.png?w=1024&amp;h=571 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1242px) 100vw, 1242px" /></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36160" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/syrian-pistachios/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png" data-orig-size="1264,686" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="syrian-pistachios" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36160" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=500" alt="syrian-pistachios"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png 1264w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=150&amp;h=81 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=300&amp;h=163 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=768&amp;h=417 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-pistachios.png?w=1024&amp;h=556 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1264px) 100vw, 1264px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The creation of food as a form of oppression of citizens, as in the starving out of wartime cities from Paris to Moscow to the Siege of Leningrad, recalling most vividly official Nazi attempts to starve out the occupied regions of the Netherlands and former Soviet Union by cutting off needed food supplies, is exactly the sort of war against civilian populations through the targeted destruction of warehouses of food that the United Nations was created to prevent:  lines of bread in war-torn eastern Aleppo grew as airstrikes destroyed Castello Road, a major avenue by which food supplies had arrived in the city&#8217;s eastern side.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36061" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png" data-orig-size="624,588" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36061 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=500" alt="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png 624w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=150&amp;h=141 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=300&amp;h=283 300w" sizes="(max-width: 624px) 100vw, 624px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>At the same time, Russian strikes that were long frustrated at their range from airports in Iran, in order to get in greater striking distance of Syria, had been frustrated by how the extended routes s both embarrassingly exposed the limits of its own air power and extended a timetable of engagement seems to have forced Moscow to develop a more effective and impressive strategy of military engagement:  the unfounded expression of <a href="http://newsrussia.xyz/russia-and-the-united-states-began-thinking-about-the-application-of-coordinated-attacks-on-aleppo/" target="_blank">hopes on Russian news agency “Interfax”</a> that “<em>Russia and the United States began thinking about the application of coordinated attacks on Aleppo</em>” and were increasingly confident of “<em>settling the situation in Syria are exploring the possibility of joint operation in Aleppo in mid-September</em>” and that “<em>those militants who were not willing to lay down their arms and withdraw from Aleppo . . . will be subject to destruction</em>” from someone &#8220;<em>close to negotiations in Geneva.</em>&#8221; If it projects a telling wish-fulfillment more than seem anything John Kerry would sign onto, the date that was selected for such a military overture is particularly striking.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36303" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/crhi1m3wyaallgo/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,710" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="crhi1m3wyaallgo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36303" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=500" alt="crhi1m3wyaallgo"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg 1200w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=150&amp;h=89 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=300&amp;h=178 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=768&amp;h=454 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=606 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36135" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/aleppo-supply-road/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png" data-orig-size="1528,1324" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="aleppo-supply-road" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36135" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=500" alt="aleppo-supply-road"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png 1528w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=150&amp;h=130 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=300&amp;h=260 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=768&amp;h=665 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=1024&amp;h=887 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1528px) 100vw, 1528px" /></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36592" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/attachment/385714397/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg" data-orig-size="300,200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="385714397" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg?w=300" loading="lazy" class=" wp-image-36592 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg?w=581&#038;h=387" alt="385714397.jpg" width="581" height="387" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/385714397.jpg?w=150&amp;h=100 150w" sizes="(max-width: 581px) 100vw, 581px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Why such a lie about joint Russian-American cooperation in an attack on Aleppo?   The air strikes that Russian Tupalove airplanes ran from Iranian soil sought to escalate their attacks with greater payloads to crush rebel strongholds in Aleppo for almost a year&#8211;Sept. 30 2015&#8211;and patience and nerves would have become frayed.  The desire to target both warehouses and convoy as it proceeded to a military zone that Russian considered to have air cover and control would have offered a strategic possibility to boost its desires.  Russian expenditures in previous years of over <a href="http://uatoday.tv/crime/prise-of-war-putin-spent-150-million-on-mercenaries-in-syria-rbc-733947.html" target="_blank">$150 million on elite mercenaries and munitions</a> in Syria&#8211;170 billion rubles&#8211;who had <a href="http://uatoday.tv/crime/prise-of-war-putin-spent-150-million-on-mercenaries-in-syria-rbc-733947.html">earlier fought in Ukraine</a>&#8211;partly funded by private investors, suggesting not only Putin&#8217;s deep personal ties to the exporting of war to the region, but suggesting the unhidden desire of Russia to establish a permanent military presence in the region, probably most desirable if located on the Turkish border.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36683" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/russian-us-plans/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png" data-orig-size="990,1122" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="russian-us-plans" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=265" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36683" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=500" alt="Russian-US Plans.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png 990w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=132&amp;h=150 132w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=265&amp;h=300 265w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/russian-us-plans.png?w=768&amp;h=870 768w" sizes="(max-width: 990px) 100vw, 990px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The parallel investment of the United States in millions of dollars of foreign aid for Syrian refugees, pledged from donor nations to the United Nations for the past five years, and suggests little faith in the &#8220;political process&#8221; or of mitigating the &#8220;relentless attacks&#8221; on Syrian civilians to which U.S. Special Envoy for Syria Michael Ratney gave particular prominence when discrediting the rumors of a joint US-Russian attack targeting Aleppo, and distancing himself from any such attacks by the Assad regime and its allies.</p>
<p>The decision to obliterate the supplies convoy in a mid-September evening continued a conscious obliteration of many structures in Aleppo, and a design to make it impossible to live in the Eastern part of the city.  Dramatically increased food shortages provide necessary background for the recent airstrikes on the convoy, as does the attempt to force a surrender by withholding food and needed supplies.  The occurrence of the attacks and their deadly damage followed and to an extent enabled by the truce that the Syrian army unilaterally declared, prompted by the US and Russia. But the destruction of supply trucks destined for Aleppo, bearing flags of the Syrian Red Crescent, supervised by Omar Barakat, show the increased ratcheting up of destructive attacks of helicopters and airplanes firing barrel bombs and shrapnel where the trucks were parked outside Syrian Red Crescent warehouses to curtailed and forestall any future delivery of further humanitarian supplies.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>8.  Could GIS overlays ever be adequate to read the escalation of Aleppo&#8217;s buildings, infrastructure, resources, and domestic residences, in the manner of those opaque but suggestive ESRI overlays whose emergence was closely tied to projects of urban renewal?  Could a map of the humanitarian disaster be created from Digital Globe images that indicate the destruction of neighborhoods, and even include human losses and human rights crimes?   To be sure, few maps can hope to register the levels of destruction used regularly on citizens of Aleppo&#8211;or the routes of airplane attack against the aid-bearing convoy that was destroyed, in an attempt to increase the bargaining chips held by the Syrian government that seeks an advantageous treaty and ceasefire during the endgame of this late stage of the Syrian Civil War.  After the route of Castello Road was effectively closed by pro-Syrian government, who first prevented delivery of food and needed supplies as advancing government positions exposed transit to sniper fire, and with the road closed from mid-July 2016, the lack of food within the city in rebel held quarters subject to rocket attacks was increasingly dire, intensifying beyond expectations what already constituted a human rights disaster.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36530" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg" data-orig-size="1024,595" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36530" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=500" alt="ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4.nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg 1024w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=150&amp;h=87 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=300&amp;h=174 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=768&amp;h=446 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" />Karam al-Masri / AFP &#8211; Getty Images</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>And so, attention turns to the destruction of the convoy bearing food to the besieged regions of the city, and the failure to explain the extent of firepower used in such unexpected targeted attacks that have effectively ended the recently brokered ceasefire.  The bombs appear dropped by two Su-24 swing-wing Russian bombers that flew from Khmeimim air base that very evening toward Syrian airspace, joining a jet-mounted chain gun with aid from Syrian army helicopters, in a targeted killing that cannot but recall the US targeted drone strikes against suspected terrorists in Pakistan or Afghanistan.  But the targets&#8211;humanitarian supplies&#8211;expand an increasing policy of starving Aleppo&#8217;s residents and depriving them of food, at the same time as the price of bread in the starting city has risen <a href="http://www.thealeppoproject.com/aleppo-conflict-timeline-2013/">twenty-fold</a>, where it can be found, from 15 US cents to over $3 (USD).</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36041" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/imrs-7-php/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg" data-orig-size="480,319" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="imrs-7-php" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg?w=480" loading="lazy" class=" wp-image-36041 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg?w=692&#038;h=460" alt="imrs-7-php" width="692" height="460" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg 480w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg?w=150&amp;h=100 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/imrs-7-php.jpeg?w=300&amp;h=199 300w" sizes="(max-width: 692px) 100vw, 692px" /><em>Karam al Masri/AFP/Getty Images</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36523" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg" data-orig-size="1024,696" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36523" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=500" alt="ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4.nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg 1024w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=150&amp;h=102 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=300&amp;h=204 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ss-160714-aleppo-syria_9_f64f7837f1f0b2e6804dcd6cec22dac4-nbcnews-ux-1024-900.jpg?w=768&amp;h=522 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Although clear lines denote the lines of hostility in the Syrian Civil War in an al Jazeera map of the former nation&#8211;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36035" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1000" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36035" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=500" alt="1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg 1200w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=150&amp;h=125 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=300&amp;h=250 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=768&amp;h=640 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1df86291d19e48cdb8c44ff75ff59394_7.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=853 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&#8211;battle lines are increasingly fluid across Aleppo, where the starvation of residents who are isolated and cut off from supplies have been long intensified through air strikes on the encircled city, in an attempt to secure the surrender of arms and all who bear them across the city&#8211;whose bombed-out eastern zones is terrifyingly evident in the Digital Globe image from late August 2016.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg"><img data-attachment-id="36619" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/figure_6syria/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg" data-orig-size="615,462" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="figure_6syria" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-36619" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg?w=630&#038;h=474" alt="figure_6syria" width="630" height="474" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg 615w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg?w=150&amp;h=113 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_6syria.jpg?w=300&amp;h=225 300w" sizes="(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px" /></a><em>Digital Globe/<a href="https://www.aaas.org/aleppo">AAAS</a> (roadblocks dismantled between August 9-23, 2016</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>9.  Indeed, the Syrian army has so persistently <a href="http://www.aljazeera.com/news/2016/09/syrian-forces-renew-siege-rebel-held-aleppo-160904170726594.html">escalated</a> its attacks on eastern Aleppo for weeks, using military bombardments to limit the entrance of any needed foods to the region&#8217;s 300,000 residents, and backed by Russian air attacks.  In recent days, images of abundance in the western part of the city have been streamed on social media, at the same time as the Syrian government forces seek to force the opposition&#8217;s hands, as the Syrian State News Agency (SANA) streams increased headlines that champion military-scale operations against the &#8220;terrorist organizations&#8221; in Homs, the southern province of Daraa, the countryside north of Hama, and to continue to destroy their weapons, <a href="http://sana.sy/en/?p=89006">boasting</a> of having launched &#8220;<em>widespread military operations against the dens of Takfiri terrorist organizations</em>&#8221; and  to have <em>&#8220;foiled an attack of ISIS terrorists&#8221;</em> signaling the collapse of the alleged cease-fire negotiated by Kerry and Lavrov in Geneva.</p>
<p>For from the early summer, Russia had continuously shelled the city of Aleppo from April.  At the same time, as pro-government forces, Iranians, and Lebanese Shi&#8217;ite militia and Hezbollah were unable to encircle it fully, airplanes flying overhead from Syria shelled the city with an intensity, <a href="http://www.reuters.com/article/us-mideast-crisis-syria-aleppo-idUSKCN0YY0PQ">promising</a> to step up its &#8220;the most active&#8221; forms of support against Aleppo falling to groups that it called &#8220;terrorists&#8221;&#8211;the catch-all category of a globalized world that blurs whatever military interests are actually at stake.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36303" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/crhi1m3wyaallgo/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,710" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="crhi1m3wyaallgo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36303" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=500" alt="CrhI1m3WYAAllGo.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg 1200w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=150&amp;h=89 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=300&amp;h=178 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=768&amp;h=454 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/crhi1m3wyaallgo.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=606 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><em>September 4, 2016</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Indeed, the strike against a UN-brokered convoy during the recent cease fire has gained attention as a violation of the US-brokered cease fire, and attacks by air and artillery against any travels on the sole road that links Aleppo&#8217;s residents in the rebel-held zones to the southern regions of the state, being unable to cut of Castello Road or the highway on the ground from Damascus.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36135" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/aleppo-supply-road/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png" data-orig-size="1528,1324" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="aleppo-supply-road" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36135" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=500" alt="ALEPPO SUPPLY ROAD.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png 1528w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=150&amp;h=130 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=300&amp;h=260 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=768&amp;h=665 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-supply-road.png?w=1024&amp;h=887 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1528px) 100vw, 1528px" /></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36137" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/highway-to-aleppo/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png" data-orig-size="1302,540" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="highway-to-aleppo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36137" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=500" alt="Highway to Aleppo.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png 1302w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=150&amp;h=62 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=300&amp;h=124 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=768&amp;h=319 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/highway-to-aleppo.png?w=1024&amp;h=425 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1302px) 100vw, 1302px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The area around Aleppo and the city itself remains a crucial if geographically displaced odd outpost over which the Syrian government needs to seek to retain control&#8211;many of whose two million residents have been subjects to repeated attacks by bombs, bunker busters, and attacks on urban infrastructure, especially in rebel-held regions, and the destruction of the many underground passageways in Aleppo–-<em>ma’aber</em> in Arabic&#8211;which the bombs targeted to isolate civilians who moved through them to acquire or purchase  food.  The convoy was struck as it approached area of the Syrian government&#8217;s control.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36061" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png" data-orig-size="624,588" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36061 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=500" alt="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png 624w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=150&amp;h=141 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624.png?w=300&amp;h=283 300w" sizes="(max-width: 624px) 100vw, 624px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The results of such bombings are not mapped with precision in a time of war, when precise aerial views are impossible to map with accuracy or comprehensiveness to convey suffering, but evident in the change in the city as seen over the past five years of attacks&#8211;much from pro-government and possibly Russian forces, who have raised the threshold on civilian attacks long before the recent attack on the civilian convoys.  From an altitude of 500 miles above the earth&#8217;s surface, the radical reduction of night-time artificial illumination around Aleppo&#8211;indicated by a red arrow in the satellite images paired below&#8211;reveal the scope of destruction in as close to an objective way as possible, if an objective image of such carnage and destruction were needed save to spare us from considering the extent of human rights violations in the city&#8217;s almost six-year siege in the ongoing Battle of Aleppo&#8211;already known four years ago as  <a class="external text" href="http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/middleeast/syria/9469080/Aleppo-is-becoming-Syrias-Stalingrad.html" rel="nofollow">Syria&#8217;s &#8216;Stalingrad.&#8217;</a></p>
<p>&#8220;Aleppo is not yet Stalingrad, or even Homs, parts of which are a wasteland of wrecked buildings,&#8221; <a class="external text" href="http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/middleeast/syria/9469080/Aleppo-is-becoming-Syrias-Stalingrad.html" rel="nofollow">wrote a journalist</a> four years ago, as the &#8220;shelling of the city began in earnest&#8221; in August 2012:  since then, the shelling with mortar and shrapnel has not only continued, but the violence ratcheted up with air bombings of increased intensity that have flattened parts of the city, now including fire-bombs and bunker-busting bombs designed to penetrate the tunnels and underground shelters where Aleppo&#8217;s citizens crowd for protection against aerial strikes.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36028" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/aleppo-at-night/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png" data-orig-size="1506,626" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="aleppo-at-night" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36028" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=500" alt="Aleppo at night.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png 1506w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=150&amp;h=62 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=300&amp;h=125 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=768&amp;h=319 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-at-night.png?w=1024&amp;h=426 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1506px) 100vw, 1506px" /><em><a href="http://www.withsyria.com/" target="_hplink">#WithSyria</a>/Digital Globe</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Images of the lit night-time skyline of Aleppo, allegedly streamed by state news media as an enticing invitation to cross to the other side, which don&#8217;t show up in this satellite image, and to surrender strongholds that the combination of Syrian government helicopters and Russian airstrikes have long attacked.  The makeshift defensive barriers and fortifications&#8211;shown by red dots, with dismantled barricades and fortified areas identified in yellow&#8211;reveal a city divided by East and West.  The ancient city of Aleppo, a UNESCO world heritage site&#8211;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg"><img data-attachment-id="36638" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/tfl_1929_aleppo_b/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg" data-orig-size="2870,2415" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="tfl_1929_aleppo_b" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-36638" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=638&#038;h=537" alt="tfl_1929_aleppo_b" width="638" height="537" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=638&amp;h=537 638w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=1276&amp;h=1074 1276w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=150&amp;h=126 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=300&amp;h=252 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=768&amp;h=646 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/tfl_1929_aleppo_b.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=862 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 638px) 100vw, 638px" /></a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png"><img data-attachment-id="36639" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/figure_22_small/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png" data-orig-size="450,348" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="figure_22_small" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png?w=450" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-36639" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png?w=633&#038;h=489" alt="figure_22_small" width="633" height="489" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png 450w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png?w=150&amp;h=116 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_22_small.png?w=300&amp;h=232 300w" sizes="(max-width: 633px) 100vw, 633px" /></a><em>Amnesty International</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg"><img data-attachment-id="36640" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/figure_23_small/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,927" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="figure_23_small" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-36640" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=617&#038;h=476" alt="figure_23_small" width="617" height="476" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=617&amp;h=476 617w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=150&amp;h=116 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=300&amp;h=232 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=768&amp;h=593 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=791 1024w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/figure_23_small.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 617px) 100vw, 617px" /></a><em>Amnesty Intenational</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&#8211;has not only been damaged extensively since 2013, from the Souq of al Medina to the Umayyad Mosque, with repeated onslaught of attacks on the city&#8217;s infrastructure, and contributed to the collapse of many ancient stone walls had collapsed and parts of the twelfth-century citadel at the heart of the medieval city, and minarets damaged on the Umayyad Mosque where snipers have taken up positions.  The burning of the Souq&#8211;a center for urban commerce from the second millennium BC&#8211;suggests a criminal death of a recently vibrant city, as well as an attack on its defenseless populations during the &#8220;continued, indiscriminate use of weaponry against its civilians&#8221;&#8211;a demand from the United States in a United Nations Security Council resolution that Russia dismissed as &#8220;totally unacceptable&#8221; and demanded to be immediately withdrawn.</p>
<p>The open attacks on civilian structures, medical facilities, and human needs in following days after the destruction of the Red Crescent convoy further ratcheted up levels of violence in the longstanding civil war.  Intensified airstrikes of &#8220;unprecedented violence&#8221; against civilian populations in coming days led to the destruction of two hospitals as Russian planes bombed areas in Eastern Aleppo, wounding hundreds and overwhelming city hospitals&#8211;and dropping incendiary  bombs intended to provoke fires in the city.</p>
<p>While UNESCO had planned a volume of the routes that children took to school through the war-torn city, the plans were cancelled since children do not now go to school; the numbers of children who have been killed in the bombing raids are not known, and probably never will, but the badly targeted and broadly based indiscriminate bombing strikes that reduce buildings to rubble as if in hopes to render the city uninhabitable.  Despite calls for war crimes prosecution from Boris Johnson, of all people, the extensive bombardment of the city, and rebel factions to demand a cease to hostilities with no Russian presence or mediation of the negotiations since it acted as a partner of Assad&#8217;s regime in perpetrating crimes against Syrians as an accomplice of the state.</p>
<p>The indiscriminate attacks against civilian inhabitants have been ratcheted up in Aleppo to a degree that has changed our thresholds of tolerance of violence from earlier years.  As it has been increasingly divided into fractured zones of control from late 2013, with civilians in &#8220;rebel&#8221; areas effectively sandwiched, pressed and isolated, encircled with power lines cut in recent months as lines of supply have been <a href="http://sana.sy/en/?p=83764">cut</a>, supposedly to restrict transit of munitions and arms to rebels who hold the region&#8211;duplicitously claiming to seek to restore <a href="http://sana.sy/en/?p=83764">safety and security</a> in the city &#8220;out of its commitment to end bloodshed&#8221; by inviting them to act by &#8220;turning in their weapons and remaining in the city or turning in their weapons and leaving it.&#8221;  Yet that <a href="http://sana.sy/en/?p=83764">purported</a> commitment to peacefulness has not prevented increasing an intensive bombardment of the divided city, and the call to&#8221;put national interest above other considerations so that security and stability can be restored to Aleppo&#8221; was, coming in late July 2016 after four years of civil war, difficult to inspire confidence as <a href="http://www.unicef.org/media/media_92027.html" target="_blank">four hospitals in Eastern Aleppo</a> were struck, disrupting health services in the besieged areas of the city in ways difficult to adequately map or obtain accurate data about.  Recent increased attacks from the air of Eastern Aleppo have come as residents are urged to avoid areas that concealed &#8220;terrorists,&#8221; in an apparent imitation of air-strikes in Afghanistan, Gaza, and Iraq, even in the face of calls to ground all Syrian war planes.</p>
<p>The current block-by-block division of the heavily barricaded city is divided most often by color-coded layers of &#8220;control&#8221;&#8211;similar to urban development maps used in redlining insurance policies in American cities by the Housing and Loan Corporation (HOLC)&#8211;but communicate little of the constantly escalating levels of violence and military attack that has undermined the urban infrastructure, as the turf wars between the Syrian Government and rebel groups has intensified, dug in, although the growth of Government Forces (shown in pink overlays below) have continued to squeeze the YPG and Islamic Front in the city but seem rolled back from the surrounding suburbs and countryside.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36113" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/aleppo-2013/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png" data-orig-size="1372,974" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="aleppo-2013" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36113" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=500" alt="Aleppo 2013.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png 1372w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=150&amp;h=106 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=300&amp;h=213 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=768&amp;h=545 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/aleppo-2013.png?w=1024&amp;h=727 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1372px) 100vw, 1372px" /><em><a href="http://www.thealeppoproject.com/aleppo-conflict-timeline-2013/">Aleppo Project/</a>source: <a href="http://caerusassociates.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Caerus_AleppoMappingProject_FinalReport_02-18-14.pdf" target="_blank">Caerus</a> p.33 (2013)</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36871" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png" data-orig-size="1302,974" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="pink-controlled-by-syrian-army" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36871" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=500" alt="Pink controlled by Syrian Army.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png 1302w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=150&amp;h=112 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=300&amp;h=224 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=768&amp;h=575 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/pink-controlled-by-syrian-army.png?w=1024&amp;h=766 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1302px) 100vw, 1302px" /><em>September 26, 2016</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Communications and transit to the &#8220;Old City are particularly fraught, surrounded is the roads and transit network with sniper fire, its surface also often destroyed by bombs.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36341" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png" data-orig-size="624,588" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="size-full wp-image-36341 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png?w=500" alt="_91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png 624w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png?w=150&amp;h=141 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/91311582_aleppo_control_19_09_16_624-1.png?w=300&amp;h=283 300w" sizes="(max-width: 624px) 100vw, 624px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The limited control over Eastern areas of Aleppo by anti-government forces belies the capture of many former government air bases around the city since 2013 that have left the government forces dependent on Russia for both bombs and airborne delivery, as a ring of air bases around the city fell into &#8220;rebel&#8221; hands aside from Aleppo&#8217;s international airport.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36096" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/air-bases/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png" data-orig-size="1364,1254" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="air-bases" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36096" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=500" alt="air-bases"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png 1364w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=150&amp;h=138 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=300&amp;h=276 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=768&amp;h=706 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/air-bases.png?w=1024&amp;h=941 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1364px) 100vw, 1364px" /></p>
<p><em><a href="http://www.thealeppoproject.com/aleppo-conflict-timeline-2013/">Aleppo Project</a></em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The delivery of supplies by road remained particularly dangerous in the past along the Damascus Road, and had ceased.  But  with most food markets now closed in the city, especially in the side held by rebel forces,</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36141" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/khanasser-road/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png" data-orig-size="1302,848" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="khanasser-road" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36141" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=500" alt="Khanasser Road.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png 1302w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=150&amp;h=98 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=300&amp;h=195 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=768&amp;h=500 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/khanasser-road.png?w=1024&amp;h=667 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1302px) 100vw, 1302px" /></p>
<p><em><a href="http://www.thealeppoproject.com/aleppo-conflict-timeline-2013/">Aleppo Project</a><a href="http://www.thealeppoproject.com/aleppo-conflict-timeline-2013/">Aleppo Project</a></em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The encirclement of Aleppo itself by government forces by late July, 2016 had made any deliveries on the corridor of Castello Road impossible, and isolated &#8220;rebel-held&#8221; regions of the city from July 27, when the divisions between East and West Aleppo .</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36145" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/july-2016-castello-road/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png" data-orig-size="1376,1428" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="july-2016-castello-road" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=289" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36145" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=500" alt="July 2016 Castello Road.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png 1376w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=145&amp;h=150 145w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=289&amp;h=300 289w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=768&amp;h=797 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/july-2016-castello-road.png?w=987&amp;h=1024 987w" sizes="(max-width: 1376px) 100vw, 1376px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The drama of Aleppo&#8217;s continued bombing is incorrectly called a &#8220;Battle,&#8221; perhaps, so much as a new struggle for Russia to insert itself within the conquest of rebels that it identifies as parties not even worth negotiating with, but only to be subdued.  Is it guided by a deep interest  to establish a military base in the region?  Or is the enlistment of Russian forces closely tied to the project of nuclear warheads that has been so dear to Assad, in ways that would change the geopolitical significance of keeping Assad in power?</p>
<p>Although the ongoing war has only apparently achieved a deep destabilization&#8211;and an inability to arrive at a resolution to the conflict outside military attacks of civilian institutions&#8211;the aim seems to be tied to Russian nuclear power plants in Syria, which have continued with Iranian and North Korean help.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>10.  At the same time as Russian planes ramped up the bombardment of the region, as if to replay the Siege of Leningrad in Syrian lands, the geopolitical stakes were considerably high:  Russian plans to construct both a massive nuclear power plant and atomic desalination plant in Syria, as well as a plutonium production reactor that seems to have been begun once again in Al-Kibar, Dair Alzour&#8211;a site once attacked by Israel with <a href="http://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-uses-17-tons-of-explosives-to-destroy-syrian-reactor/">seventeen tons of explosives</a>, constructed with North Korean and Iranian help, is currently possibly being rebuilt as a site of uranium storage; the reporting of a potential underground nuclear facility near the Lebanese border by <em>Der Speigel</em>&#8211;admittedly unclear in satellite imagery&#8211;is reportedly the site to which 8,000 fuel rods received in 2007 for the destroyed plant have been <a href="http://www.haaretz.com/middle-east-news/.premium-1.636310">transferred</a>, where they are guarded by Hezbollah allies of the beleaguered Syrian government.  The continued cultivation indicates Assad&#8217;s continued tenacious cultivation of a commitment to nuclear facilities in Syria.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36374" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/attachment/3968476195/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg" data-orig-size="1218,685" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="3968476195" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36374" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=500" alt="3968476195.JPG"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg 1218w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=150&amp;h=84 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=300&amp;h=169 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=768&amp;h=432 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/3968476195.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=576 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1218px) 100vw, 1218px" /></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36445" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/ap071024069123-635x357/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg" data-orig-size="635,357" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="ap071024069123-635&#215;357" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36445 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg?w=500" alt="AP071024069123-635x357.jpg"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg 635w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg?w=150&amp;h=84 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/ap071024069123-635x357.jpg?w=300&amp;h=169 300w" sizes="(max-width: 635px) 100vw, 635px" /><em>Satellite images of al-Kibar reactor, AP/Digital Globe, before and after Israeli attack</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The rapid dismantling of and bulldozing at the site prevented inspection of the facilities and may have intentionally concealed what it had developed at the site, visible on the publicly accessible imagery of Digital Globe, perhaps revealing the excavation of buried lines to the former reactor.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36455" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg" data-orig-size="474,193" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6&#215;2" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg?w=474" loading="lazy" class=" wp-image-36455 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg?w=661&#038;h=269" alt="071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2" width="661" height="269" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg 474w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg?w=150&amp;h=61 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/071026_syria_hlg_3p-grid-6x2.jpg?w=300&amp;h=122 300w" sizes="(max-width: 661px) 100vw, 661px" /></p>
<p><em>GeoEye/Digital Globe&#8211;Images of September, 2003; Aug. 10, 2007 before air attack; October 24, 2007.</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The existence of site of possible weaponization seem to threaten attack by their geographic proximity to Israel, which precipitated the strike at al-Kibar before the site was active.  Nuclear weapons systems present a means for Bashar to preserve military parity with Israel, indeed, in hopes counterbalance his regime&#8217;s weak military forces.  They may provide a basis for his similar tenacity in Aleppo&#8217;s destruction:  Assad&#8217;s duplicitous 2009 statement to &#8220;<em>want a nuclear-free Middle East, Israel included</em>&#8221; foregrounded these fears.  And after Argentinian and Indian offers to help with construction of nuclear reactors were withdrawn in the 1990s, fears of Chinese assistance in weaponizing fissile materials in later years, the emergence of a 2003 deal with Russians to build both a nuclear power plant and nuclear seawater desalination plant have opened the feared specter of technology transfer that Assad has long desire, and diverted funds&#8211;a specter that grows with the lack of access to the sites of the International Atomic Energy Agency as Civil War has prevented security conditions for inspections and given rise to recent fears that the up to fifty tons of uranium Syria seems to possess that may be enriched may fall into Al Qaeda hands.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36238" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/marj_as_sultan_figure_1/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg" data-orig-size="847,818" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="marj_as_sultan_figure_1" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36238 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=500" alt="Marj_as_Sultan_Figure_1.JPG"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg 847w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=150&amp;h=145 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=300&amp;h=290 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/marj_as_sultan_figure_1.jpg?w=768&amp;h=742 768w" sizes="(max-width: 847px) 100vw, 847px" /><em><a href="http://isis-online.org/isis-reports/detail/satellite-image-shows-suspected-uranium-conversion-plant-in-syria1/14">Suspected Uranium Conversion Plant in Syria-Institute for Science and International Security /ISIS</a>, 2008</em></p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36422" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/mainana/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png" data-orig-size="616,394" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="mainana" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png?w=500" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-36422 aligncenter" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png?w=500" alt="mainana.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png 616w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png?w=150&amp;h=96 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mainana.png?w=300&amp;h=192 300w" sizes="(max-width: 616px) 100vw, 616px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The existence off a feared &#8220;underground facility&#8221;&#8211;perhaps near Qusayr, just two kilometers from Lebanon&#8217;s border&#8211;reported by <em>Der Spiegel</em>&#8211;may be incorrect, and should be named with a question mark, rather than asserted in a red frame&#8211;but centers of nuclear enrichment have been identified in Homs and the existence of a secret underground reactor&#8211;code name &#8220;Zamzam,&#8221; named after the well God created for Abraham&#8217;s wife and son in the desert&#8211;using the 8,000 rods from the previously destroyed nuclear reactors.  At the time of the 2008 inspection of the Kibar nuclear facility Israeli planes had destroyed in late 2007, Syria rebuffed requests of the IAEA to visit three sites suspected to be capable of enrichment&#8211;including <a href="http://isis-online.org/isis-reports/detail/satellite-image-shows-suspected-uranium-conversion-plant-in-syria1/14#images" target="_blank">Marj al-Sultan</a>, Hama, and Homs, the latter of two have since fallen to ISIS&#8211; by the US-based Institute for Science and International Security (the &#8220;other ISIS&#8221;); the Syrian government&#8217;s flat refusal to allow the visits raised eyebrows about the possible existence of whether a secret cache of up to 50 tons of natural uranium hidden from observers and the danger of proliferation it posed, despite official disclaimers of the presence in the country of any nuclear fuel&#8211;and the uncertainty has been argued to work to Syria&#8217;s advantage.  Syria&#8217;s denial of potential sites of enrichment sites revealed by satellite tracking, near a city now fallen to rebel troops, may conceal its relocation in time to escape its detection to a site from which frequent calls have been tracked to the head of the Syrian Atomic Energy Commission, Ibrahim Othman, near the &#8220;Zamzam&#8221; site, nearby the Lebanese city of Qasr where an underground military site seems maintained by Hezbollah with Iran&#8217;s help.</p>
<p>The involvement of Russia in the construction of such potential sites of nuclear reactors, however, threatens to suggest a scary dimension for Russia&#8217;s dissimulation of its intent in the region&#8211;and a deeper danger of bombing any regions held by Syria&#8217;s government, if not a basis for the continued confidence of Bashar al-Assad as his airfare seems to seek to continue to bomb his country, which lies increasingly in ruins.  Is the onslaught in Aleppo the cost of Bashar&#8217;s tenacity in being able to pursue his nuclear plans, a hope for which he has almost sacrificed his cities under the pretense of fighting alleged terrorists?</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="36264" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg" data-orig-size="745,599" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-36264" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg?w=500" alt="image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg 745w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg?w=150&amp;h=121 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image-797304-galleryv9-nnju-797304.jpg?w=300&amp;h=241 300w" sizes="(max-width: 745px) 100vw, 745px" /><em><a href="http://www.spiegel.de/international/world/evidence-points-to-syria-still-working-on-a-nuclear-weapon-a-1012209.html">Der Spiegel</a> (2015)</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Does the promise for may underlie the continued bombardment of Aleppo to rubble, in a bizarre mapping of the bombed-out ruins of the city onto the fear of nuclear proliferation?  A recent  report that five nuclear engineers&#8211;including an Iranian&#8211;<a href="https://now.mmedia.me/lb/en/NewsReports/564380-iranian-nuclear-engineer-killed-in-damascus" target="_blank">were assassinated</a> north of the Syrian capital, Damascus, while on route to a declared nuclear research center in Barzeh, a reactor developed with Chinese help, suggests the dedication of energy to broad networks to bolster Syria&#8217;s nuclear capacity to which Russia may be closely tied.  Fears that Iran and Hezbollah are occupying central roles in the running the sites of nuclear facilities in the south of Syria&#8211;and some to <a href="http://www.jewishpress.com/indepth/analysis/j-e-dyer/an-iranian-nuclear-weapons-program-in-what-was-formerly-syria/2015/01/18/">fear</a> that Iran has been running its own nuclear program within the country.  While the ancient and modern residential buildings alike of the city of Aleppo are destroyed by bunker-buster bombs which often bury their former inhabitants, and have forced most of the city&#8217;s inhabitants to flee, after calls for all &#8220;bearing arms&#8221; to surrender their weapons and <a href="http://sana.sy/en/?p=83764" target="_blank">quit or remain in the city</a>, the clear annihilation of Aleppo from above seems a terrible augur for a power eager to develop nuclear weapons.</p>
<p>While we often have mapped the terrifying displacement of millions of Syrian refugees during the ongoing civil war, to try to conjure and measure its costs, calmed by the presence of humanitarian assistance on the ground in many of the regions&#8217; largest cities, the virtual disappearance of Aleppo&#8217;s buildings is a parallel delocatiion, altering forever one&#8217;s relation to the city as a place.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg"><img data-attachment-id="37094" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/syrian-refugee-crisis-2/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg" data-orig-size="460,378" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="syrian-refugee-crisis" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg?w=460" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter  wp-image-37094" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg?w=521&#038;h=428" alt="syrian-refugee-crisis" width="521" height="428" srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg 460w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg?w=150&amp;h=123 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/syrian-refugee-crisis.jpg?w=300&amp;h=247 300w" sizes="(max-width: 521px) 100vw, 521px" /></a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-attachment-id="39284" data-permalink="https://dabrownstein.com/2016/09/28/finding-aleppo/soros_1-111016/" data-orig-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg" data-orig-size="1600,1067" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="soros_1-111016" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=500" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-39284" src="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=500" alt="soros_1-111016.png"   srcset="https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg 1600w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=150&amp;h=100 150w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=300&amp;h=200 300w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=768&amp;h=512 768w, https://dabrownstein.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/soros_1-111016.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=683 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /><em><a href="http://www.nybooks.com/articles/2016/11/10/on-bombing-aleppo/">Abdalrhaman Ismael/Reuters</a></em></p>
